msgid "Enable Cache Headers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:345
msgid "Send Cache-Control, Surrogate-Keys, and Vary headers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:349
msgid "Dynamic Content (HTML)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:353
msgid "Pages, posts, archives, REST API — generated by PHP. These headers are sent by the plugin directly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:357
#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:389
#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:498
msgid "CDN TTL (s-maxage)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:360
msgid "seconds. Default: 172800 (48h). How long Varnish keeps HTML pages."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:364
#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:396
#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:505
msgid "Browser TTL (max-age)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:367
msgid "seconds. Default: 3600 (1h). Reduces unnecessary checks to CDN nodes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:372
msgid "Homepage (front page)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:376
msgid "The homepage is the most-requested URL and the one that must never fall back to the origin. Give it its own policy — a short fresh window plus a generous stale-while-revalidate — so an expiry is served stale instantly while a single request revalidates behind it, instead of a miss storm. When off, the homepage uses the global HTML profile above."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:380
msgid "Dedicated homepage profile"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:384
msgid "Use these values for the homepage instead of the global HTML TTLs"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:392
msgid "seconds. Default: 300 (5 min). Short fresh window for a news homepage."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:399
msgid "seconds. Default: 30. Low so breaking news is picked up quickly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:403
msgid "Stale-while-revalidate"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:406
msgid "seconds. Default: 300. After expiry the edge serves the stale homepage instantly and a single request revalidates behind it — this is what shields a weak origin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:410
msgid "Stale-if-error"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:413
msgid "seconds. Default: 86400 (24h). Airbag: if the origin returns 5xx, serve the last good homepage instead of an error."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:420
msgid "Serve-stale VCL (grace / keep) — propose-only, makes stale-while-revalidate actually work"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:421
msgid "The homepage profile sends stale-while-revalidate and stale-if-error, but Varnish only serves stale during revalidation when grace/keep match. This snippet derives them from the Cache-Control the plugin sends, so they stay in sync. The plugin never deploys VCL — copy it into Configuration → VCL."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:423
#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:954
#: includes/admin/views/tab-security.php:130
#: includes/admin/views/tab-speculation.php:133
msgid "Copy VCL"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:430
msgid "Origin page cache (serves HTML before WordPress boots)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:434
msgid "On a CDN miss the edge still has to fetch from the origin. This serves a pre-rendered copy of anonymous pages before WordPress boots, so that fetch does not regenerate WordPress. Enable/disable it from the Page Cache card at the top. Logged-in users, and any URL or cookie in your exclusions, are never page-cached."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:438
msgid "Storage backend"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:443
msgid "Disk (default)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:444
msgid "Zero dependencies, works anywhere. Each lookup is a filesystem read, so on slow or network disk (NFS) and under very high concurrency the I/O and stat cost shows, and lookups index slower than an in-memory store."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:448
msgid "Redis"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:449
#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:455
msgid "Available"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:449
msgid "Redis detected but password-protected — set WP_REDIS_PASSWORD in wp-config.php."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:449
msgid "Redis server detected, but the phpredis extension is not installed — selecting this would cache nothing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:449
msgid "Redis is configured but not answering — start the service or check WP_REDIS_HOST / WP_REDIS_PORT."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:449
msgid "Not available on this server — selecting this would cache nothing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:450
msgid "In-memory key lookup, no disk I/O: faster under concurrency and better at indexing than disk. Reuses your WP_REDIS_* settings. Requires the Redis service and the phpredis extension."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:454
msgid "Memcached"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:455
msgid "Memcached server detected, but the PHP extension is not installed — selecting this would cache nothing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:455
msgid "Not available here — needs the Memcached PHP extension and a running server; selecting it would cache nothing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:456
msgid "Same in-memory advantage as Redis; its flush is generation-based so it never wipes a store shared with the object cache. Requires the Memcached service and extension."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:459
msgid "Change the backend, then toggle the Page Cache off and on from the card above to apply it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:463
msgid "Page cache TTL"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:466
msgid "seconds. Default: 300. It is only a fallback for edge misses, so a short value is fine; a purge clears it anyway."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:471
msgid "Object cache (protects logged-in users and wp-admin)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:475
msgid "Page cache only covers anonymous visitors. Your editors, and every wp-admin and admin-ajax request, bypass it and hit the database directly. A persistent object cache (Redis or Memcached) absorbs that load. Without one, a busy newsroom can overwhelm MySQL even with page cache on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:479
msgid "Automatic"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:483
msgid "Enable the object cache automatically when a live memory backend (Redis or Memcached) is detected"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:485
msgid "Recommended. When off, you must enable the object cache by hand from the card at the top. It never overwrites an object-cache.php from another plugin without your confirmation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:490
msgid "Static Resources (CSS, JS, images, fonts, video)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:494
msgid "Static files are served by the web server, not PHP. The plugin sets Cache-Control headers so Varnish respects these TTLs from the origin. When assets change (media uploads, theme/plugin updates), the plugin invalidates them automatically."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:501
msgid "seconds. Default: 2592000 (30 days)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/main-page.php:508
msgid "seconds. Default: 86400 (1 day)."
msgstr ""

